[tool], is, in the catalog
    if [tool], returns, [anything]
[command], is, named as a command
    if [command], uses, [any tool], [any input]
    and [command], starts with, "command: "

[command], breaks, Every command uses a tool in the catalog
    if [command], uses, [tool], [any input]
    and not [tool], is, in the catalog
[command], breaks, Every command is named as a command
    if [command], uses, [any tool], [any input]
    and not [command], is, named as a command

a command with a tool nobody has, adds line, workflow.plain, "command: guess, uses, guess, x"
a command with a tool nobody has, must break, Every command uses a tool in the catalog

a command not named as a command, adds line, workflow.plain, "list it, uses, list, the folder"
a command not named as a command, must break, Every command is named as a command

[command], breaks, Every tool returns only what the catalog lists
    if [command], returned, [field], [any value]
    and [command], uses, [tool], [any input]
    and not [tool], returns, [field]

a command with two tools, adds line, workflow.plain, "command: a mix-up, uses, list, the folder"
a command with two tools, adds line, workflow.plain, "command: a mix-up, uses, find go comments, tools.go"
a command with two tools, must break, Every tool returns only what the catalog lists

[file], is, used
    if [anyone], loads, [file]
[file], is, used
    if [file], is, part of the machine

[file], breaks, Every file is used
    if [file], is, in the folder
    and not [file], is, used

a file nobody uses, adds line, notes.plain, "a, is, a note"
a file nobody uses, must break, Every file is used

[file], breaks, Every file engine.go loads is in the folder
    if engine.go, loads, [file]
    and not [file], is, in the folder

a missing workflow, adds line, spec.plain, "engine.go, loads, missing.plain"
a missing workflow, must break, Every file engine.go loads is in the folder

[file], has a rule for, [word]
    if [rule], is in, [file]
    and [rule], defines, [word]

[file], breaks, Each word has one creator
    if [file], has a rule for, [word]
    and [fact pattern], names, [word]
    and [creator], creates fact, [fact pattern]
    and [creator], differs from, [file]

a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, adds line, workflow.plain, "command: a fake, returned, file, nowhere"
a workflow that fakes what the tools returned, must break, Each word has one creator

a spec that looks for itself, adds line, spec.plain, "ghost.txt, is, in the folder"
a spec that looks for itself, must break, Each word has one creator

"engine.go, loads, spec.plain", means in mangle, 'loads("engine.go", "spec.plain").'
"spec.plain, is, in the folder", means in mangle, in_the_folder("spec.plain").
a law is broken, means in mangle, a_law_is_broken().
"command: list the folder, uses, list, the folder", means in mangle, 'uses("command: list the folder", "list", "the folder").'
"[file], is, used", means in mangle, used(File).
"[any file], is, used", means in mangle, used(AnyFile).
"true, exits with, 0", means in mangle, 'exits_with("true", 0).'
'a change, adds line, notes.plain, "a, is, a note"', means in mangle, 'adds_line("a change", "notes.plain", "a, is, a note").'
"[file], ends with, [ending]", means in mangle, ":string:ends_with(File, Ending)"
"[command], starts with, [prefix]", means in mangle, ":string:starts_with(Command, Prefix)"
"[file], differs from, [other file]", means in mangle, File != OtherFile
'[command], is the join of, "command: find the comments in ", [file]', means in mangle, 'Command = fn:string:concat("command: find the comments in ", File)'

[line], breaks, Every line reads back as written
    if [line], is, misread

a line that reads back differently, adds line, spec.plain, '"zzz", means, nothing'
a line that reads back differently, must break, Every line reads back as written

a hand-written declaration, adds line, spec.plain, "declared: [line], is, misread"
a hand-written declaration, must break, Every line reads back as written

.plain, means, plain language
.go, means, go
go.mod, means, go module
go.sum, means, go checksums
.sh, means, sh

